# imagemagick: renders the hicolor icon sizes from the single 512x512 master in
# debian/ (see debian/rules). The package name is the same on every series; only
# the CLI name differs (IM6 `convert` vs IM7 `magick`), which rules resolves.
# unzip: debian/rules unpacks the CLI and GUI release zips upstream publishes.
# They reach the source tree through the .dsc's Debtransform-Files instead of a
# merged tarball we would have to assemble and host, so the unpacking is ours.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               libicu-dev,
               imagemagick,
               unzip
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/SabreTools/MPF
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation

Package: mpf
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         mpf-check (= ${source:Version}),
         mpf-cli (= ${source:Version}),
         mpf-gui (= ${source:Version})
Description: Media Preservation Frontend suite (metapackage)
 Media Preservation Frontend (MPF) is a suite of tools that drives the
 optical-media dumping workflow used by the Redump preservation project:
 .
   * mpf-check  log validator + submission-info writer
   * mpf-cli    headless dump orchestrator
   * mpf-gui    Avalonia desktop frontend
 .
 This metapackage installs all three. Install the individual packages if you
 only need part of the suite.

Package: mpf-check
Architecture: amd64
# Self-contained .NET binary: dh_shlibdeps sees only the apphost's own NEEDED,
# so the dlopened .NET runtime libs are declared by hand (parity with the RPM).
# ${dep:icu} is filled per-series at build (libicu74 noble / libicu70 jammy).
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${dep:icu},
         libkrb5-3,
         libgssapi-krb5-2,
         libssl3,
         zlib1g,
         libunwind8,
         jq
Description: Validator that generates Redump !submissionInfo.txt from dump logs
 MPF.Check reads the log files next to a finished optical-media dump and
 writes a !submissionInfo.txt alongside in the Redump submission format.
 Supported dump sources include redumper, Aaru, DiscImageCreator, Cleanrip
 and UmdImageCreator.
 .
 Optional copy-protection scanning is available via --path/--scan; it inspects
 the files on the mounted medium and needs no privileges beyond read access to
 them.
 .
 Self-contained .NET binary, repackaged unchanged from the upstream rolling
 release.

Package: mpf-cli
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${dep:icu},
         libkrb5-3,
         libgssapi-krb5-2,
         libssl3,
         zlib1g,
         libunwind8,
         jq
Recommends: redumper732, aaru5, discimagecreator
Description: Headless dump orchestrator (drives redumper, aaru, discimagecreator)
 MPF.CLI orchestrates the disc-dumping workflow from a terminal: it drives the
 selected backend (redumper, aaru or discimagecreator) through the dump,
 post-processes the output and writes the submission info.
 .
 MPF needs no elevated privileges: it never talks to the drive directly. The
 raw SCSI access belongs to the backend dumper, which carries the cap_sys_rawio
 capability on its own binary and receives it regardless of who starts it. The
 bundled Programs/ dumper folder from the upstream zip is dropped at package
 build time in favour of the system-installed dumpers; mpf-cli resolves the
 backend binary via PATH (seeded into ~/.config/mpf/config.json by the wrapper).
 .
 Self-contained .NET binary, repackaged from the upstream rolling release.

Package: mpf-gui
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${dep:icu},
         libkrb5-3,
         libgssapi-krb5-2,
         libssl3,
         zlib1g,
         libunwind8,
         jq,
         hicolor-icon-theme,
         desktop-file-utils
Recommends: redumper732, aaru5, discimagecreator,
            libx11-6, libice6, libsm6, libxext6, libxi6, libxrandr2,
            libxcursor1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6
Description: Avalonia desktop frontend for the MPF disc-dumping workflow
 MPF.Avalonia is the desktop GUI of the MPF suite. It drives the disc-dumping
 workflow with a graphical interface built on Avalonia (.NET cross-platform UI
 toolkit).
 .
 The GUI runs unprivileged: it never talks to the drive directly, and the
 backend dumper it spawns carries the cap_sys_rawio capability on its own
 binary. Granting the capability to the GUI itself would break every file
 dialog, because a process with file capabilities is non-dumpable and
 xdg-desktop-portal then cannot identify it. The bundled Programs/ dumper
 folder is dropped at build time in favour of the system-installed dumpers,
 resolved via PATH.
 .
 Avalonia 11.x ships only the X11 backend; on Wayland sessions the GUI runs
 through Xwayland. The X11 runtime libraries are weak dependencies so headless
 installs of the other subpackages stay lean.
 .
 Self-contained .NET binary, repackaged from the upstream rolling release.
